11. Management Review and Objectives

Toward the end of the meeting, Drew referenced a previously sent email regarding ISMS objectives.

He noted that management review should include:

* ISMS objectives
* Metrics used to assess achievement of those objectives
* Metrics related to ISMS performance monitoring
* Updates to the risk assessment and associated improvement work

Drew emphasized that these are not separate workstreams, but closely connected components of effective ISMS governance and management review preparation.

⸻

12. Decisions and Agreements

The following conclusions and agreements were reached during the meeting:

1. The current ISMS risk register requires additional refinement this year.
2. The risk register must be maintained as a living document and included in management review.
3. The team will conduct a structured exercise to compare SOA controls against risk-linked controls.
4. Missing control-to-risk mappings will be identified and resolved.
5. New risks will be added where necessary, with particular attention to:
    * Physical security
    * AI
    * Climate and external disruption
    * Cybersecurity standards compliance
6. Existing AI governance structures, such as the DUEGC, should be documented and referenced where appropriate.
7. The objectives and metrics work should be incorporated into management review preparation alongside the risk assessment updates.

